The image attached shows several data types, including ATAC, RNA, and Hi-C data. ATAC data shows us the accessibility of chromatins.
Non-coding OCRs are areas of the gene that are not made into proteins but contain important sites for gene regulation.
Hi-C loops show us how specific DNA locations interact to form a loop. These loops are essential for gene regulation since they bring genetic material closer to each other, which may contain regulatory elements.
To summarize, the data shown helps us examine how genetic material interacts and how it is regulated by promoters, enhancers, or silencers.
